l.syntax/prod? 1] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term 1] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- 2] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/readable-term- 3] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/rebinder 3] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/subst- 4] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/term-reduce 3] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/top-assumption 1] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.syntax/vars 1] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.typing/generalize-params 2] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.typing/prepare-argument-subst 6] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-app 4] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-args 3] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-refdef 5] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! 1] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.utils/map-with 3] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.utils/vconcat 2] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.utils/vcons 2] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\", [latte-kernel.utils/zip 1] \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\"}\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:178:`F` not reducing to a Π is Reject (R-APP, `:not-a-function`). `A' ≢ A` is Reject (R-APP, `:argument-mismatch`).\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:191:**Rule R-CHECK.** `E; Γ ⊢ t : T` iff `E; Γ ⊢ t ⇒ T'` and `E; Γ ⊢ T' ≡ T`. The checker never guesses a type for `t` from `T`; there is no bidirectional refinement in v1. Failure of the conversion is Reject (R-CHECK, `:type-mismatch`) and reports both `T'` and `T` in weak head normal form.\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:245:3. Compare heads: `sort` by L-4; `bvar` by index; `const` with the same name by L-4 on levels, then on mismatch unfold either side by C-4 if transparent and retry; `app` spines by head then pairwise arguments by C-9; `lam` and `pi` by domain then body under the extended context; `let` after zeta.\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:270:**Rule O-4 (no host contribution).** Nothing the executing VM does, no primitive result, no effect and no continuation operation contributes a step to §4. If the kernel's execution encounters a host failure, the outcome is a harness failure, reported outside O-1, never a `Reject`.\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:304:**Example D-c.** `theorem bad [] T (lam (sort zero) (lam (bvar 0) (bvar 1)))` into `·`: Reject (R-CHECK, `:type-mismatch`). The body returns `P`, of type `sort zero`, where `bvar 0`, of type `P`, is required.\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:331:3. During a check the configuration is frozen (kernel plan §5). Any VM-level event that would alter it, a registry extension, a primitive redefinition or a store write outside the checker's own state, is a harness failure under O-4.\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:356:Each fixture records the expected pair of outcomes. A mismatch with the recorded pair blocks; a match with Lean is neither required nor expected.\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:377:`Accept` and `Reject` compare as above. A Yin `Unknown` never matches any oracle outcome and blocks a fixture that claims completed checking. A Lean resource exception is recorded as the oracle's `Unknown`, distinct from a Lean type error. A broken driver, translator or crashed process is a harness failure, not a negative fixture.\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:387:| F-5 | R-APP mismatch: `app t (sort (succ zero))` with `t` from §3.5 | Reject (R-APP) |\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:388:| F-6 | R-LET annotation mismatch | Reject (R-LET) |\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:18:| `semantic.scan-test` (then `semantic-register.scan-test`) C4 golden mismatch (JVM, Node) | slow tier at 355bd84b | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed 2026-10-14: the `[:c4 :py]` scanner golden regenerated mechanically after the other seat's linker relocation | P2 |\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:24:| `semantic/frame.cljc` (formerly :141; now ~:159) compares a captured frame's free-environment bindings with the task's free-env by host `=`; not NaN-reflexive on JS/Dart (a NaN-valued free binding in a captured/parked/waiting frame would be `:free-env-mismatch` there; same class as the 8f-3 NaN fix) | 8f-3 NaN ruling §5 | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed on branch `srvm-frame-nan` (Architect signed off; the commit is the one adding `bindings=` to frame.cljc): guarded slotwise content equality; JVM focused 116 tests / 1380 assertions and quick tier 4007 tests / 249662 assertions green, host-equality mutant 9 failures; [evidence](../collab/yin-vm/1792082835156-engineer-frame-nan.report.md) (Node/Dart lanes assigned to orchestrator) | P3 |\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:42:| `yin.vm.values` hashes a `Contin