int `cED`, PHP because the trace holds the argument (corner C30), yang.php because of this leak | P4 S5 independent review (codex gpt-6.1-sol round 2, P2) and Architect sign-off condition 5, restated by the 17.3 ruling of 2026-10-28; `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc` parameter initialization | yang.php | P4 S6 (cover parameter initialization in the unwinding cleanup so every acquired parameter is released on failure); fixture `:decl-byref-later-rejection-releases-earlier-param` (`#{:p4-s6}`) | P2 |\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:574:| yang.php C30: exception traces hold no arguments, so an argument rejected at acquisition is released at the throw where PHP keeps it alive until the exception is freed (departure `cDE` vs `cED`) | 17.3 ruling 2026-10-28 on oracle pass 9; design section 17.2 C30 | yang.php | none scheduled; a trace-frames slice | P3 |\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:576:| yang.php: a later rejected by-reference argument leaked an earlier parameter's acquisition (`function f(D &$a, int &$b)`, `$a = new D`, `$b = 'bad'`: PHP prints `cDE` once the trace is freed, yang.php printed `cED`); closed in P4 S6: declared parameter types are checked in the body's prologue (`php/check-param-cell!`), inside the cleanup that releases every parameter cell, and a function with a typed parameter always takes the unwinding cleanup path. Without freeing the exception both print `cED` (corner C30) | P4 S5 independent review (codex gpt-6.1-sol round 2, P2) and Architect sign-off condition 5, restated by the 17.3 ruling of 2026-10-28; `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc` parameter initialization | yang.php | closed in P4 S6; fixture `:decl-byref-later-rejection-releases-earlier-param` (enabled) | P2 |\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:580:| yang.php: `exit`/`die` is refused (`:constant`), so row 51 (`exit` inside a destructor proceeds to shutdown, corner C9) cannot run; fixture `:obj-row51-exit-in-destructor` is authored and gated by `:p4-exit` | checkpoint B audit (fixture package); desi