tores its original\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3891:`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3893:exception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3900:source exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3905:Each activation establishes its own exception bridge and saves its\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3910:or exception does so before common propagation under its own rules.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3917:inner exception as specified in section 8.10.7.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3968:exceptions, effects, suspension, and identity. Correctness must not\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3989:   exception boundaries under the entry. Keep existing source `:call`\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4020:  required/extra arguments, keyword errors, receivers, exceptions, and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4054:  propagation. Assert original exception identity and cleanup order,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4291:coercions, collections, and language exceptions.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4394:6. Retain no exception, recognizer, token, or host stack object in\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4493:surfaces as a deterministic guest exception (C3 ruling 11).\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4598:- Java numeric and exception semantics.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4701:9. **Semantic preservation:** observable values, mutation, exceptions,\n34:                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n37:                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n38:                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n---\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\n---\n\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\n\n## Domain Scope\n\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\n\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\n\n## Delegation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: Lead System Architect\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\n\nRead first:\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\n- <target-design-file>\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\n\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\n```\n| yang.clojure: `library-for` counts only `defn` as a program definition; a `def`/`defn-`/`defmacro` redefinition of a library name over-pulls the library definition (harmless, the program definition wins); closing route: share the compile-program defined-names scan | slice 7 review (glm), fix round | yang.clojure | slice 8 | P3 |\n| yang.clojure: `apply` surface gaps against Clojure, e.g. `(apply :k [{:k 1}])` fails loudly where Clojure returns 1; closing route: lower a keyword or collection operator in apply to the static lookup | slice 7 review (glm), fix round | yang.clojure | open | P3 |\n\n\n## Closure notes: test-strategy-feedback-contract (2026-10-29)\n\nThe original TS-P3 rows above remain unchanged. Fixes are in `a475d775`.\n\n- **TS-P3-01: closed.** The docs route runs `git diff --check HEAD -- <paths>`\n  over staged and unstaged content together. Paths absent from `git ls-files`\n  print `unchecked (untracked)`, appear under `:unchecked` in the EDN scope\n  record, and leave `:gate-complete? false`. Real temporary-repository regression\n  probes cover fully staged whitespace errors, staged plus unstaged content,\n  untracked docs, and mixed tracked/untracked docs. Real `bb test:routed` runs\n  also confirmed the staged docs gate and the untracked warning/scope.\n- **TS-P3-02: closed.** Routing and quick-sharded print machine-readable EDN\n  verification-scope records with `:scope`, `:exit`, `:dry-run?`, and\n  `:gate-complete?`; the final JVM `summary.edn` includes the same record.\n  Foundation/JVM-only feedback always leaves `:gate-complete? false`, including\n  exit 0. Empty selections print `0 JVM namespaces selected` and exit 1, also\n  in dry runs. Self-tests cover nonempty feedback, empty selections, dry runs,\n  failed children, failed process launch, and failed prerequisites. A real\n  `bb test:routed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` run selected 61 JVM namespaces:\n  993 tests, 15,833 assertions, zero failures/errors; both runner scope records\n  reported exit 0 with `:gate-complete? false`. This is JVM feedback, not a\n  G2/G3 tri-host completion claim.\n- **TS-P3-03: closed.** `build-n-test.md` now names the Node REPL build\n  prerequisite (`build:yin-repl-node`) as the prerequisite that ensures\n  `bb deps:npm`.\n\nVerification: `bb -cp src/dev -m quick-sharded-test` passed 9 tests and 141\nassertions with zero failures/errors. Lint on the three changed Clojure files\nreported zero errors/warnings; `cljstyle check` passed. The requested\n`clj -M:kondo --lint src/dev` reported 31 errors and 27 warnings in unrelated\nfiles. Linting an archived `1fe3eb07` baseline produced identical findings;\nthose pre-existing Jolt/probe findings are outside this contract's file scope.\n| yang.typescript/yang.php: the JS and Dart ANTLR parser targets are deliberately not built — parsing is JVM-only, and the checked-in CST packets are the portability boundary (Node/Dart execute parserless). The cross-host parse plan (collab/1793127916000-reviewer-crosshost-parse-plan.gpt-6-luna.findings.md and the astra reconciliation 1793128437000) is retired as a declined capability: no JS/Dart parser for either frontend exists today (the manifests declare `:java` only), so nothing was built against the granted helper-port licensing. Python keeps its multi-target parsers (`:java`/`:javascript`/`:dart`/`:cpp`, the J2b zero-pin record) as its own lane's capability, which creates no obligation for the other two | owner ruling 2026-10-30 (\"don't build the JS/Dart parser except on the JVM\"); `antlr/typescript/manifest.edn` and `antlr/php/manifest.edn` declare `:java` only; `build/antlr/{typescript,php}/` contain no js/dart output; `antlr/python3/manifest.edn` declares all four targets and J2b closed at zero pins | yang.typescript/yang.php (this seat) | none scheduled — a live browser REPL parsing user-typed source would be the only reopening case, and the demo runs samples parserless from packets | P3 |\n| jolt ws: a ping after a local close is queued gets no pong (A4 \"every ping produces one pong\" holds until a local close exists) | pump.jolt:597 (handle-event! :ping guard); wave-1 Architect sign-off P3 | jolt (J6) | documented behaviour, closed by J6e's docstring sentences; J6h cites the archived sign-off | P3 |\n\n\n## Clojure common-call arbitration dispositions (2026-10-30)\n\nAppend-only disposition of Kimi r4. The two recorded deviations stand;\nthis entry does not alter or retire existing ledger rows.\n\n+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
