{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files /Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs | rg 'latte.*(proof|presyntax|syntax|norm|nbe|typing|defenv|utils)\\\\.cljc\"'$'\"'; sed -n '1630,1675p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; git show daef60da -- docs/agents/known-gaps.md\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/presyntax.cljc\n/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/nbe.cljc\n/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/defenv.cljc\n/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/utils.cljc\n/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/syntax.cljc\n/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/proof.cljc\n/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/typing.cljc\n/Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/norm.cljc\n  [{:keys [call guest-call definitions project-proof?]} guest?]\n  (let [env (if guest? initial-context 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\n        register (if guest? 'register-definition 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition)\n        env (reduce (fn [env definition] (list register env (if guest? (kernel-call definition) definition))) env definitions)\n        call (if guest? (kernel-call (or guest-call call)) call)\n        call (if project-proof?\n               (list 'let ['r call] '(if (= :ok (first r)) [:ok (rest (second r))] r)) call)]\n    (list 'let ['env env] call)))\n\n\n(defn- evidence-data\n  \"EDN evidence retains all portable values and metadata. Nonportable host\n   payloads are explicit evidence, not accepted representation differences.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (fn? x) {:nonportable-host-value (str (class x))}\n    (record? x) (evidence-data (upstream-record-data x))\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(evidence-data k) (evidence-data v)])) x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv evidence-data x)\n    (set? x) (set (map evidence-data x))\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map evidence-data x))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-attempt\n  [f]\n  (try (f)\n       (catch Exception e\n         {:status :blocked :message (ex-message e)\n          ;; Observer exceptions attach the entire host VM as :session. It is\n          ;; diagnostic machinery, not a portable domain payload; recursively\n          ;; expanding its closure environments duplicates the whole program.\n          :data (evidence-data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session))\n          :host-session-attached? (contains? (ex-data e) :session)\n          :causes (mapv (fn [cause] {:class (str (class cause)) :message (ex-message cause)})\n                        (take-while some? (iterate ex-cause e)))\n          :exception (str (class e))})))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-a\n  [fixture]\n  (kernel-attempt\n    #(let [value (cond\n                   (#{:opacity-proof :opacity-install} (:mode fixture))\n                   (let [outcome (a-opacity-proof (:script fixture) (= :opacity-install (:mode fixture)))]\n                     (if (= :ok (first (:value outcome)))\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-17vmDSIP' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-02 14:31:32.294 xcodebuild[23741:105352120]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-02 14:31:32.573 xcodebuild[23741:105352119] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-DIsfm3RJ' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-02 14:31:33.268 xcodebuild[23758:105352167]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-02 14:31:33.502 xcodebuild[23758:105352166] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ncommit daef60da2f7ebba73b6bd301b1768071d110d237\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Fri Oct 30 01:43:53 2026 +0700\n\n    fix(yang.clojure): preserve fresh supply through have steps\n    \n    Carry rebuilt type contexts through the enclosing have branch and bind the caller context in check-proof. Cover named and anonymous have steps, inferred types, immutable prior contexts, declarations and proof continuation on both VM lanes.\n    \n    Append the four deferred P3 findings and their closing obligations verbatim to the known-gaps ledger.\n    \n    Validation: 143 tests, 2230 assertions, zero errors and only the intentional kernel-gate failure; all 24 new regression assertions pass. Kondo has zero errors and the same two inherited warnings. Formatting and whitespace checks pass.\n\ndiff --git a/docs/agents/known-gaps.md b/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\nindex e44fce22..9f027e2f 100644\n--- a/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n+++ b/docs/agents/known-gaps.md\n@@ -175,3 +175,30 @@ reported zero errors/warnings; `cljstyle check` passed. The requested\n `clj -M:kondo --lint src/dev` reported 31 errors and 27 warnings in unrelated\n files. Linting an archived `1fe3eb07` baseline produced identical findings;\n those pre-existing Jolt/probe findings are outside this contract's file scope.\n+\n+\n+## Hardening2 round-1 P3 dispositions (2026-10-30)\n+\n+These four P3 items are deferred this round; closing obligations retained below\n+verbatim from the round-1 review. P2 fresh-supply propagation is the sole code\n+fix in this round. Source: [round-1 review](../../collab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md).\n+\n+1. Deferred; owner seat: yang.clojure. Finding and closing obligation:\n+\n+> **P3 | src/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj:50-57** | The stale manifest generator still rewrites `test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn` in the old schema (no `:disposition`/`:admission-reason`), while `latte-oracle-tables/-main` (src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:48-51) is now the writer of record. Running the old tool per its own docstring (`clj -M -m latte-oracle-manifest`) wipes the admission inventory from the working tree; the schema assertion in `test-oracle-classification` (test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:281-283) then fails loudly, but the checked-in inventory is lost and the old header comment is now false. | Fix: delete `latte-oracle-manifest` or reduce it to a delegation to `latte-oracle-tables`, and update its docstring.\n+\n+2. Deferred; owner seat: yang.clojure. Finding and closing obligation:\n+\n+> **P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:895-919** | The portable `try` lowerer's catch arm fires on *any* `[error-tag v]`: it binds `(data/nth outcome 1)` (line ~912) without discriminating the thrown value. A thrown non-ex-info value (e.g. `(throw \"boom\")` inside `(try … (catch Exception e …))`) is caught by the guest but propagates in Clojure (a thrown String is not an Exception). The catch-class guard (lines 903-905) constrains only the *syntax* of the clause, not the runtime class of the thrown value. Unexercised: all kernel sources throw ex-info only, and `test-portable-try-outcomes` (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2024) tests ex-info throws exclusively. | Fix: either record the limitation in the library notes next to the other \"known compromises\" (clojure.cljc:1908-1916), or discriminate at runtime (catch only values carrying `:yin.k/message`, re-propagating others).\n+\n+3. Deferred; owner seat: yang.clojure. Finding and closing obligation:\n+\n+> **P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1163-1166** | Callable collections route through `invoke-value` only when the operator is a **local** or a **non-symbol** (`(or (contains? (locals env) operator) (not (symbol? operator)))`). A top-level defined collection — `(def v [1 2]) (v 0)` — compiles to a plain `:application` and errors at runtime instead of indexing, diverging from Clojure. Untested boundary of the \"callable collections\" admission (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2049 uses only `let`-bound collections). | Fix: record as a known boundary in the library notes, or extend the route to operators in `::defined`.\n+\n+4. Deferred; owner seat: yang.clojure. Finding and closing obligation:\n+\n+> **P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1918-1926** | `kind-arities` publishes `'var? [1]` unconditionally (line 1926) while `kind-module` provides `var?` only under `#?(:clj … :default {})` (line 1920) — on a Node/Dart host the arity profile would admit a binding the module cannot supply. Relatedly, metadata attached via the new `kind/with-meta` seam has no stated serialization-survival guarantee: no fixture round-trips a meta'd value through the store/encoder, so `meta` after restoration is unspecified. | Fix: gate the published arity with the same reader conditional (or register the capability per-host at harness setup), and add a note/obligation that host metadata is not a serialized ABI field.\n+\n+Additional closing condition, verbatim:\n+\n+> Conditions: findings 1's cross-host arity drift and the metadata-serialization obligation above should be tracked as explicit follow-ups before the owed Node/Dart lanes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
