he astra reconciliation 1793128437000) is retired as a declined capability: no JS/Dart parser for either frontend exists today (the manifests declare `:java` only), so nothing was built against the granted helper-port licensing. Python keeps its multi-target parsers (`:java`/`:javascript`/`:dart`/`:cpp`, the J2b zero-pin record) as its own lane's capability, which creates no obligation for the other two | owner ruling 2026-10-30 (\"don't build the JS/Dart parser except on the JVM\"); `antlr/typescript/manifest.edn` and `antlr/php/manifest.edn` declare `:java` only; `build/antlr/{typescript,php}/` contain no js/dart output; `antlr/python3/manifest.edn` declares all four targets and J2b closed at zero pins | yang.typescript/yang.php (this seat) | none scheduled — a live browser REPL parsing user-typed source would be the only reopening case, and the demo runs samples parserless from packets | P3 |\n181-| jolt ws: a ping after a local close is queued gets no pong (A4 \"every ping produces one pong\" holds until a local close exists) | pump.jolt:597 (handle-event! :ping guard); wave-1 Architect sign-off P3 | jolt (J6) | documented behaviour, closed by J6e's docstring sentences; J6h cites the archived sign-off | P3 |\n182-\n183-\n--\n195-|                               |                                                   | fails. No VM type, descriptor seal, or provenance registry. Equal immutable    |\n196-|                               |                                                   | reconstructions retain the same value.                                         |\n197-+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n198:| (d) constant stack: restored  | test-outcome-common-call-depth: named and mutual  | Every source callee is admitted before common invocation. Constructor entries  |\n199-|                               | calls, walker and semanti